# CODEOWNERS for tellahq/eks-node-monitoring-agent (fork of aws/eks-node-monitoring-agent)
#
# Any path that requires explicit reviewer approval — particularly anything
# that affects CI authority (workflows touching OIDC, secrets, ECR pushes) —
# must list owners here. Branch protection on tla_main has
# `require_code_owner_reviews: true`, so PRs touching these paths cannot
# merge without an approving review from a listed owner.

# Default: any change to the fork needs an explicit reviewer.
*                                  @tellahq/developers

# CI / OIDC / publish authority — extra-sensitive. Anything in here that
# triggers on push, dispatch, or schedule has the ability to assume the
# github-actions-ecr OIDC role and push images to our ECR.
/.github/                          @tellahq/developers
/.github/workflows/                @tellahq/developers
/.github/workflows/tla-*.yaml      @tellahq/developers

# Dockerfile and build inputs feed the published image. A malicious change
# here could ship a backdoored binary even if the workflow itself is clean.
/Dockerfile                        @tellahq/developers
/go.mod                            @tellahq/developers
/go.sum                            @tellahq/developers

